      <h2>Introduction to Computer Networking</h2>

      <p>
        Computer networking allows devices such as computers,
        smartphones, and servers to communicate and share
        resources. Networks can range from small home networks
        to large systems that connect millions of devices
        across the world.
      </p>

      <p>
        Networks are an essential part of modern technology.
        They allow people to access websites, exchange emails,
        share files, and use online services. Without computer
        networking, many of the technologies we rely on
        every day would not be possible.
      </p>

      <h3>How Do Networks Work?</h3>

      <p>
        Computer networks use hardware devices and communication
        protocols to transfer data between connected systems.
        Routers, switches, and wireless access points help
        devices connect, while protocols establish the rules
        for exchanging information.
      </p>

      <p>
      <strong>Source</strong><br>
